Z||000000||fieroburton||08-06-2001||06:24 PM||||selling my 84  to buy a newer car. I want a vette or a 87 fiero gt <BR>can somebody tell me what are the specs of a gt like acceleration time 0-60 , 1/4 mile time ? <BR>do fiero gt's feel deferent than a 84 ?<BR>just tell me all about them <BR>thanks alot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    [img]www.geocities.com/fieroburton/25_25.jpg[/img]<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||08-06-2001||06:46 PM||||I'm not a book full of stats, but there is a difference, a big one, between an 84 and a GT. The 84 I believe ran 0-60 in something just over 11 seconds, the other 4 cyls in 10.6.<BR>The Fiero GT runs it in 8 seconds or so, although there are claims of mid 7 stock times. Depends on whether its a manual or auto, how good a driver you are, etc.  The 85 GT is also the fastest of the stock GTs. 88s are the slowest of the GTs.<P>A Vette is most likely going to be faster, but a Fiero cheaper. I don't know prices or times on Vettes, or if you want your speed from a strictly stock car, but a lot of it is just driver opinion.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000002||saleenfiero||08-06-2001||06:50 PM||||What kind of vette were you talking about?  Most likely the only ones you're gonna find in the same price range as a fiero GT would be the lamented late 70's early 80's vettes.  They are 12 for 10 cents around here, but still look nice.  They are also quite slow, if you're talking other years, like if you are torn between a 2002 Z06 or a fiero GT, I'm sorry, I'm gonna have to say get the Z06.||||reg||1
