Z||000009||FieroKyle||08-06-2001||11:06 PM||||Alright, here is my opinion. I like vettes but only certain years. I like the 50's, 60's, and early 70's Vettes the best, and then late 90's and the new Z06s. The 80's and early 90's I think are the worst Vettes. A decent Vette is gonna run you 10K to 15K from the 80's and late 70's. A good Fiero is gonna run you 3K to 6K, depending on mileage and condition and so forth. So just put a V-8 in the Fiero which would run about 10K comes to anywhere from 12K to 16K. Plus the Fiero would probably be more superior in performance than the Vette with the V-8. But the Vette is a lot more than just a car like a Fiero its just not another car. I like Fieros more than Vettes, but thats because I own one. I would go based on what you can find for the best deal for the car. In my opinion, I would take the Vette. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroKyle||08-06-2001||11:10 PM||||One other thought, if I had the money to buy a Vette right now, I wouldn't, I would buy stuff for my car for better performance and looks. I would get a V-8. Suspension package, (lowering and other goodies). Totally re-upholster it (not like it is at all bad, but there are spots I don't like. Modify my stereo I have in it just a bit. And wallah! A better car than a Vette.||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||08-07-2001||12:02 AM||||just like said already......everywhere you go you see Vetts. There like the Taurus of sports cars. I like being different.||||reg||1
Z||000012||California Kid||08-07-2001||12:36 AM||||It's a decision only you can make!!!<P>But remember the vette is going to cost you more in insurance, every year!!!<P>Secondly, how are you going to feel when a Fiero "blows" you off ???<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Pontiaddict||08-07-2001||01:19 AM||||If you can't afford to put a v8 into a Fiero, how can you afford a Corvette?<BR>Unless you buy a Corvette from the smog years, a stock Fiero shouldn't have a chance given the driver of the Vette knows what he's doing.<BR>GT's do feel different than 84's. It feels like you're driving a bigger more powerfull car.(which you are). I think that I had more fun with my 84 than I do driving my GT though. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||FieroKyle||08-07-2001||12:37 PM||||Nah, I changed my mind. The Fiero anyday.||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||08-07-2001||02:41 PM||||Fiero... the early C4s had electrical issues.. and the Trans (auto) computers often failed.. my former boss had a few and loves his C5 but hated all 5 C4s he had. guess he didn't learn the first 2 times and my near stock 300zx-tt would SMOKE him... <A HREF="http://www.corvetteforum.com" TARGET=_blank>www.corvetteforum.com</A>  poke around there... but i still say Fiero... easier to work on, cheaper parts, and cheaper insurance than the C4. or a C3 78-82 those are fun (my first car was a 79   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Muncie 4spd, Holley 900 3 barrel.. stupid cops...i wasn't speeding HONEST! ) but 90% are over $10,000 and if you drop $10,000 in a fiero you'll have a less obvious and less common ride<P>just my $.02...<P><BR>or if you can find an 83 on e-bay or somwhere.. JUMP ALL OVER IT..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">           <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
